.Dd $Mdocdate: October 27 2026 $
.Dt FUGUWEBRC 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fuguwebrc
.Nd site description of fuguweb
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The description is
.Pa .fuguwebrc
at the project root.
It is UTF-8, and a description that is not fails the load.
A setting is one
.Ar name No = Ar value
line.
A block opens with its type, a name, and a brace, and closes with a
brace on a line of its own.
A name that holds whitespace takes double quotes.
A block with a language tag in front of its name is a translation, and
.Sx LANGUAGES
states its rules.
A
.Ql #
starts a comment, and no value can hold one.
The description holds the words of the default language.
.Pp
The settings are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "module_root" -offset indent
.It Ic site
The site name of each language whose block names none.
It ends the title of each page of such a language, and it is the text
of the banner link.
This setting is required.
.It Ic url
The absolute URL of the site root.
It starts with
.Ql https://
or
.Ql http:// ,
and it ends in a solidus.
This setting is required.
.It Ic footer
The footer fragment of each language whose block names none, below the
source directory.
A description with no
.Ic footer
gives a site with no footer.
.It Ic out_dir
The output directory.
The default is
.Pa web/build .
.It Ic source_dir
The source directory.
The default is
.Pa web .
It must not name the project root, such as
.Pa \&.
or
.Pa ./ .
The project root holds the record of
.Sx TRANSLATION STATUS ,
and the build publishes each plain file of the source directory.
.It Ic entry
The front page of each language tree, and the target of the banner
link.
The default is
.Pa index.html .
.It Ic module_root
The prefix that a module name drops.
The default is
.Pa lib .
.It Ic man_url
The manual host for a cross-reference to a manual outside the site.
The default is
.Lk https://man.openbsd.org/ .
.It Ic stylesheet
The path of the base stylesheet.
By default the build searches for the sheet that ships with the tool.
.El
.Pp
A path setting must not step out of the project.
.Pp
The block types are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic language Ar tag
One language of the site.
See
.Sx LANGUAGES .
.It Ic nav Qq Ar href
One navigation entry, in file order.
Every page carries it, except the forward
.Pa index.html
at the top level.
A relative
.Ar href
names a page of each tree, such as
.Pa manuals.html ,
and an absolute URL stays as it stands.
The block must set a
.Ic label .
.It Ic page Qq Ar file
One page of each language tree, named by its file in the tree.
The name must be one path segment.
The block sets a
.Ic title ,
which defaults to the file name, and exactly one source:
.Bl -tag -width "markdown" -offset indent
.It Ic body
An HTML body fragment in the source directory.
.It Ic markdown
A Markdown file, relative to the project root.
.Xr lowdown 1
renders it, and the HTML that it holds stays as written.
.It Ic index No = Cm yes
The generated manual index.
The page can also set a
.Ic body ,
which opens the index below its heading.
.El
.Pp
.Ic unlinked No = Cm yes
marks a page that no other page links to, such as
.Pa 404.html ,
and the reachability check skips it.
.It Ic manuals Ar name
One group of
.Xr mdoc 7
manuals.
The name is one word of lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, and it is
the fragment identifier of the group on the index page.
Two groups must not share a name.
The block must set
.Ic heading ,
the text of the heading of the group, and
.Ic dir ,
the directory of the sources.
An optional
.Ic namespace
prefixes each manual name, so
.Pa man/fugu/Daemon.3p
with the namespace
.Ql Fugu:\&:
becomes
.Ql Fugu::Daemon(3p) .
.It Ic modules Ar name
One group of POD sidecars.
The name follows the rules of a
.Ic manuals
name.
The block must set
.Ic heading
and
.Ic dir ,
and
.Ic dir
must lie below
.Ic module_root .
.It Ic keys Qq Ar name
One published key directory.
A description can hold several, and two blocks must not name one
directory.
See
.Xr fuguweb-keys 7 .
.El
.Pp
The load fails for a block type or a setting that this manual and
.Xr fuguweb-keys 7
do not document, and the message names the block and the word.
A setting of an older description fails the same way.
The load fails when a block names no source or two sources, when two
blocks name one page, or when a group directory does not exist.
It fails when two manuals, or a manual and a
.Ic page
block, become one page.
Each test of two names that become one page folds the two, as
.Xr fuguweb-site 7
states.
It fails when the path of a source from the project root holds ASCII
white space or a parenthesis.
A source is a page source, a manual or a footer fragment, of any
language.
A symlink at the top level of the source directory fails the load.
A symlink below the source directory on the path of a fragment that the
build reads fails it too.
A group block whose name is no group name fails the load.
Every message names the file and the block at fault.
.Sh LANGUAGES
A
.Ic language
block declares one language of the site.
The block name is the tag of the language, and the order of the blocks
is the order of the languages.
The first language is the default.
A description with no
.Ic language
block has the one language
.Ql en .
.Pp
A tag is a BCP 47 tag, in its canonical case: a language subtag of two
or three lowercase letters, then an optional script subtag such as
.Ql Hans ,
then an optional region subtag such as
.Ql BR
or
.Ql 419 .
.Ql en ,
.Ql zh-Hans
and
.Ql pt-BR
are tags.
.Pp
The settings of a
.Ic language
block are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "footer" -offset indent
.It Ic name
The name of the language in that language, such as
.Ql English .
This setting is required.
.It Ic dir
The direction of the language:
.Cm ltr
or
.Cm rtl .
The default is
.Cm ltr .
.It Ic site
The site name in this language.
The default is the
.Ic site
of the description.
.It Ic footer
The footer fragment of this language, below the source directory.
The default is the
.Ic footer
of the description.
.El
.Pp
A translation is a block with the tag of a declared language in front
of its name.
The tag must not be the tag of the default language.
The block translates the block of one argument of the same type and
name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
language en {
	name = English
}

language de {
	name   = Deutsch
	footer = de/footer.body.html
}

page "index.html" {
	title = Home
	body  = index.body.html
}

page de "index.html" {
	title = Start
	body  = de/index.body.html
}

manuals commands {
	heading = Commands
	dir     = man/fuguweb
}

manuals de commands {
	heading = Befehle
	dir     = man/de/fuguweb
}
.Ed
.Pp
The build writes one tree for each language, below the tag in
lowercase, and each tree holds the same pages.
The tree of
.Ql zh-Hans
is
.Pa zh-hans/ .
A
.Ic page ,
a
.Ic nav ,
a
.Ic manuals
and a
.Ic modules
block can take a translation:
.Bl -tag -width "manuals, modules" -offset indent
.It Ic page
.Ic title ,
.Ic body
and
.Ic markdown .
.It Ic nav
.Ic label .
.It Ic manuals , modules
.Ic heading
and
.Ic dir .
.El
.Pp
A page of a language takes each value of its translation, and the value
of the default block where the translation holds none.
The site name and the footer of a language follow the same rule.
Each value records the language that it comes from, and the page
layout of
.Xr fuguweb-site 7
marks a value of another language than the page.
.Pp
The
.Ic dir
of a group translation mirrors the default
.Ic dir .
A manual of a language comes from the file of the same relative path in
that directory, and from the default source when the directory holds no
such file.
A
.Ic modules
translation mirrors the umbrella sidecar as well.
A manual keeps the page name of its default source in every language.
.Pp
A page of another language than the default must hold the outline of
its page in the default tree: the same count of headings, at the same
levels, in the same order.
Each heading then takes the id of the heading at the same position of
that page, or no id when that heading has none.
Each link of the page to one of its headings names the new id.
A section reference of a manual,
.Ql \&.Sx ,
finds its heading by its text, and each other link by its old id.
A link to a heading that takes no id stays as it stands.
A link to a fragment of a page then works in each language.
A page whose outline differs fails the build, and the message names the
page, the language and the position of the first heading that differs.
.Pp
The load fails when a tag has another shape, or when two blocks declare
one tag.
It fails when a
.Ic language
block has no
.Ic name ,
or a
.Ic dir
of another word.
It fails when a translation names a tag that no
.Ic language
block declares, or the tag of the default language.
It fails when a translation names no default block of its type, when it
comes twice for one name and one language, or when it sets a setting
outside its list.
It fails when a manual source of a translation
.Ic dir
has no source of the same path in the default
.Ic dir .
A
.Ic language ,
a
.Ic keys
and a
.Ic key
block take no translation.
.Sh TRANSLATION STATUS
A translation follows its source, and a source changes.
The record
.Pa TRANSLATIONS
at the project root names the version of the default source that each
translated file follows.
The build and the check do not read the record.
.Pp
The record holds one line for each translated file, in the form of a
SHA256 manifest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
SHA256 (web/zh-hans/index.body.html) = <digest>
.Ed
.Pp
The path names the translated file from the project root.
It holds no
.Pa \&./
step, no empty step and no final solidus, so a path setting of
.Pa ./web
or
.Pa web/
gives the path
.Pa web/zh-hans/index.body.html .
The digest is the SHA-256 of its default source at the time of the
translation.
The lines sort by path.
A record that is absent or empty holds no line.
.Pp
.Cm translated
writes the line of each
.Ar file ,
with the digest that the default source of that file has now.
It changes each
.Ar file
to the form of a path of the record, so
.Pa ./web/a.html
and
.Pa web/a.html
name one file.
It keeps each other line of the record.
It refuses a file that translates no source of the description, such as
a default source, and then it writes nothing.
.Pp
Two parts that name one translated file must name one default source,
because the record holds one digest for each file.
.Cm status
and
.Cm translated
refuse a description that does not obey this rule, and name the file
and the two sources.
.Pp
.Cm status
prints one line for each part of a language other than the default
that does not follow its source.
A line holds four fields, with one tab between two fields: the tag of
the language, the state, the kind of the part, and its name.
The lines follow the order of the languages, and then the order of the
description.
.Pp
The states are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "unrecorded" -offset indent
.It Cm fallback
The part comes from the default language.
.It Cm unrecorded
The language translates the file, and the record holds no line for it.
.It Cm stale
The line of the file names a digest other than the one that its
default source has now.
.El
.Pp
The kinds of part, and the name of each, are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "heading" -offset indent
.It Cm site
The site name.
Its name is the tag of the language.
.It Cm label
The label of a
.Ic nav
entry.
Its name is the href of the entry.
.It Cm title
The title of a page.
Its name is the name of the page.
.It Cm page
The source of a page.
Its name is the name of the page.
.It Cm heading
The heading of a group.
Its name is the name of the group.
.It Cm manual
The source of a manual.
Its name is the page of the manual.
.It Cm footer
The footer fragment.
Its name is the tag of the language.
.El
.Pp
The site name, a label, a title and a heading are values of the
description, and a value is
.Cm fallback
or follows its source.
A file part follows no source when the default language names none for
it, and it then takes no line.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fuguweb 1 ,
.Xr fuguweb-keys 7 ,
.Xr fuguweb-site 7
